# The single biggest product change

Cairn needs to stop presenting itself as:

> **“a sophisticated sync system with a UI”**

and become:

> **“a normal folder that quietly solves the studio's file problem.”**

The user should mostly experience:

```text
Choose folder
↓
Ready
↓
Work normally
↓
Files appear elsewhere
↓
Need one locally?
Make available
↓
Need client feedback?
Share review link
```

Everything else — FastCDC, CAS, BLAKE3, FUSE/CfAPI, leases, journals, P2P, STUN, FEC, protocol versions, WAL, merge classifiers — should be doing its job **without requiring the user to know it exists**.

That is the largest remaining ROI in Cairn.

And importantly, **the new ADR-0030 work means I would not rewrite the architecture to get there**. The direction is now much better: keep the core, finish the authority/state model, and put a much stronger product boundary over it.
